0,Emberá languages - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emberá_languages,"Eperara (Epena): Joaquincito, Cajambre, Naya, Saija, Tapaje, Satinga Ethnologue (2005, 2009) treats Tadó (*) as a separate language. A case can be made for classifying Baudó in the Northern Embera group. It has many features of both groups and is partially intelligible with the neighboring Northern Embera dialect as well as with Epena.",Embera Tadó,Chocoan
