8,Eperara language - grokipedia.com,https://grokipedia.com/page/eperara_language,"The Eperara language, also known as Epena or Emberá-Saija, belongs to the Chocoan language family, a small indigenous language group primarily spoken along the Pacific coast of Colombia and Ecuador. Within this family, Eperara is classified under the Embera branch, which comprises a dialect continuum of closely related varieties.",Embera Tadó,Chocoan
